From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:15:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] connman: let wpa_supplicant decide optional PMF

ConnMan 1.42 sends ieee80211w=1 for WPA2/WPA3 transition networks. An
explicit per-network value skips wpa_supplicant's check for BIP support
in the driver. The rtl8821cs driver of the H700 image has no BIP, so it
negotiates PMF with a PMF-capable access point and then fails:

  WPA: Failed to configure IGTK to the driver
  RSN: Failed to configure IGTK

and disconnects itself right after the group handshake, before DHCP.

Carry the 1.42 backport of the ConnMan fix that sets the per-interface
global Pmf=1 instead (as NetworkManager does), so wpa_supplicant keeps
optional PMF where the driver has BIP and drops it where it does not.
SAE-only networks keep ieee80211w=2. Backport by marekjalovec
(knulli-cfw/knulli-linux#115) of Batocera's patch; upstream:
https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260919-pmf-fix-v1-1-a84bab14eb34@outlook.fr
---
 ...optional-pmf-via-global-pmf-property.patch | 82 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 82 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 board/patches/connman/001-gsupplicant-enable-optional-pmf-via-global-pmf-property.patch

diff --git a/board/patches/connman/001-gsupplicant-enable-optional-pmf-via-global-pmf-property.patch b/board/patches/connman/001-gsupplicant-enable-optional-pmf-via-global-pmf-property.patch
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..3c966d6f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/patches/connman/001-gsupplicant-enable-optional-pmf-via-global-pmf-property.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+From: Ilyas <ilyas.tasli@outlook.fr>
+Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 15:43:40 +0200
+Subject: [PATCH] gsupplicant: Enable optional PMF via global Pmf property
+
+Commit 5e73b55e ("gsupplicant: Set MFP optional and key_mgmt for PSK")
+sets ieee80211w=1 on every PSK network. When ieee80211w is set
+explicitly, wpa_supplicant uses it as is and skips its check for BIP
+support in the driver. That check only runs when PMF comes from the
+global pmf setting.
+
+Drivers without any BIP cipher, e.g. iwlwifi/iwldvm (Centrino
+Wireless-N 2230, Advanced-N 6205/6235), therefore negotiate PMF with
+PMF-capable APs and then fail to install the IGTK:
+
+  nl80211: kernel reports: key setting validation failed
+  wlan0: WPA: Failed to configure IGTK to the driver
+  wlan0: RSN: Failed to configure IGTK
+
+The station then deauthenticates locally right after the 4-way
+handshake, so it can no longer connect to WPA2 networks it used to
+connect to before 1.45.
+
+Set the per-interface global Pmf property to "1" instead and stop
+adding ieee80211w to PSK networks. MFPC is still advertised on
+hardware that supports PMF, as intended by 5e73b55e. wpa_supplicant
+disables PMF itself when the driver lacks BIP. NetworkManager uses
+the same approach (NetworkManager commit a9ab50ef, "supplicant: set
+optional PMF using global supplicant property").
+
+Upstream: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260919-pmf-fix-v1-1-a84bab14eb34@outlook.fr
+
+[Backported to 1.42, where ieee80211w=1 is only set for WPA3-Personal
+transition mode networks. ieee80211w=2 is kept for SAE-only networks.]
+---
+diff --git a/gsupplicant/supplicant.c b/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
+index 1b92ec4..d8a5b48 100644
+--- a/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
++++ b/gsupplicant/supplicant.c
+@@ -2539,6 +2539,13 @@ static GSupplicantInterface *interface_alloc(const char *path)
+ 	return interface;
+ }
+ 
++static void set_pmf(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
++{
++	const char *pmf = user_data;
++
++	dbus_message_iter_append_basic(iter, DBUS_TYPE_STRING, &pmf);
++}
++
+ static void interface_added(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
+ {
+ 	GSupplicantInterface *interface;
+@@ -2562,6 +2569,15 @@ static void interface_added(DBusMessageIter *iter, void *user_data)
+ 	if (!interface)
+ 		return;
+ 
++	/*
++	 * Enable optional PMF through the per-interface global setting
++	 * instead of per-network ieee80211w=1, so that wpa_supplicant
++	 * disables it when the driver does not support any BIP cipher.
++	 */
++	supplicant_dbus_property_set(path, SUPPLICANT_INTERFACE ".Interface",
++				"Pmf", DBUS_TYPE_STRING_AS_STRING,
++				set_pmf, NULL, "1", NULL);
++
+ 	if (!properties_appended) {
+ 		supplicant_dbus_property_get_all(path,
+ 						SUPPLICANT_INTERFACE ".Interface",
+@@ -4963,12 +4979,11 @@ static void add_network_security(DBusMessageIter *dict, GSupplicantSSID *ssid)
+ 				 * WPA2-Personal (PSK) and WPA3-Personal (SAE)
+ 				 */
+ 				key_mgmt = "SAE WPA-PSK";
+-				ieee80211w = G_SUPPLICANT_MFP_OPTIONAL;
+ 			} else {
+ 				key_mgmt = "SAE";
+ 				ieee80211w = G_SUPPLICANT_MFP_REQUIRED;
++				add_network_ieee80211w(dict, ssid, ieee80211w);
+ 			}
+-			add_network_ieee80211w(dict, ssid, ieee80211w);
+ 		} else {
+ 			key_mgmt = "WPA-PSK";
+ 		}
